        "date": "2026-11-22T10:12:30Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(boundary): separate inside and outside boundary offsets\n\nThe one Boundary offset moved both lines of an open boundary: the line\nthat the user picked and the stock side. A negative value to cut less\nair also moved the picked edge. AreaControls gets outer_offset for the\nouter line; offset now moves only the picked line (or the whole closed\narea). Equal values run the old law exactly. An old project file loads\nits one offset into both and saves the same bytes. The Boundary group\nshows two rows, and set_operation_area takes outer_offset.\n\nFixes #3338\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
